_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/state.json" "file_sha256" "baea455fb2924dc2cf1299d5f2336376c259449922c26af6dc859032416a3c87"} {"question" "q-333727" "field" "field-8" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/state.json" "file_sha256" "baea455fb2924dc2cf1299d5f2336376c259449922c26af6dc859032416a3c87"} {"question" "q-333727" "field" "field-8" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "phase portrait"] ["text" "vector field"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/state.json" "file_sha256" "baea455fb2924dc2cf1299d5f2336376c259449922c26af6dc859032416a3c87"} {"question" "q-333727" "field" "field-8" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "phase portrait"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/state.json" "file_sha256" "baea455fb2924dc2cf1299d5f2336376c259449922c26af6dc859032416a3c87"} {"question" "q-334279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/assets/4be4e2001c6c2f499ea95b932ba600772827ca5ce4df2abedb629ac5d4daee75.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two complex eigenvalues $\\lambda =a\\pm b\\text{i}$ is shown above. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.The given curve is \n{{field-1}},\nrepresenting\n{{field-2}}\nthat is traversed \n{{field-3}}.\nThus, we must have \n{{field-4}}.\n\nThe spiral is traversed toward \n{{field-5}}\nas $t\\to \\infty .$\nHence, \n{{field-6}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/state.json" "file_sha256" "baea455fb2924dc2cf1299d5f2336376c259449922c26af6dc859032416a3c87"} {"question" "q-334279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow notice that the given curve is $\\text{unbounded},$ representing $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$ Thus, we must have $a\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, notice that the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{the origin}.$\n\nHence, to insure that ${e}^{at}\\to 0,$ we require $a<0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/state.json" "file_sha256" "baea455fb2924dc2cf1299d5f2336376c259449922c26af6dc859032416a3c87"} {"question" "q-334279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "85d6cc71a17ffa258f3fef4d69c46a490d6a247f7c9046f246e70752f10489cc"} {"question" "q-334279" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/state.json" "file_sha256" "baea455fb2924dc2cf1299d5f2336376c259449922c26af6dc859032416a3c87"} {"question" "q-334279" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "bounded"] ["text" "unbounded"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/state.json" "file_sha256" "baea455fb2924dc2cf1299d5f2336376c259449922c26af6dc859032416a3c87"} {"question" "q-334279" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "unbounded"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/state.json" "file_sha256" "baea455fb2924dc2cf1299d5f2336376c259449922c26af6dc859032416a3c87"} {"question" "q-334279" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/state.json" "file_sha256" "baea455fb2924dc2cf1299d5f2336376c259449922c26af6dc859032416a3c87"} {"question" "q-334279" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "a spiral"] ["text" "an ellipse"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/state.json" "file_sha256" "baea455fb2924dc2cf1299d5f2336376c259449922c26af6dc859032416a3c87"} {"question" "q-334279" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "a spiral"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" 